    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:mission-analytics-dashboard-v1-2-0:assignment:1",
      "name": "Pipeline and environment recon",
      "description": "Read-only inventory for this mission: (a) how `scripts/build.py` and `scripts/aflib/model.py` copy a skill's `scripts/` subfolder into `dist/` for all four targets, and whether `.py` files pass through untransformed; (b) every file that mentions the report outputs or the report flow (`src/skills/mission-report/SKILL.md`, `src/agents/black-agent.md`, `src/commands/start-mission.md`, the OpenCode command mirror, the Codex and Antigravity operating manual) and which are generated; (c) the exact JSON shape that `maturity.py summary --json` and `.actionboard/registry.json` runs provide, including `completed_at`; (d) which tests assert dist file lists or counts and so will need updating when a new script is added; (e) whether the guard or any hook blocks Black Agent from writing `*.html` or `mission-metrics.json`; (f) every place version 1.1.0 is declared (already seen: `src/VERSION`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`, `packages/installer/package.json`, `packages/installer-py/pyproject.toml`, `packages/installer-py/actionboard_install/__init__.py` and `__main__.py`) and any others; (g) the file inventory of `~/.claude/skills/hallmark/` (SKILL.md, `references/dark-mode.md`, `data-viz.md`, `responsive.md`, `gates.md`) with each rule's relevance to this dashboard; (h) Chrome and Edge executable paths, Node and Python 3.9–3.12 availability, and whether `--log-net-log` works headless; (i) freshness of `./graphify-out/` against HEAD.",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:green"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/PotentialActionStatus",
      "result": {
        "@type": "DefinedTerm",
        "name": "acceptance",
        "description": "A recon report with a table for each of (a)–(i), each reference carrying a file path and line number, and a yes/no answer for (e). Files created/changed: none."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:mission-analytics-dashboard-v1-2-0:assignment:2",
      "name": "Dashboard renderer and metrics collector",
      "description": "Create `render_dashboard.py` with two subcommands. `metrics` writes `mission-metrics.json` from `--started-at`, `--ended-at`, `--git-base <ref>` (via `git diff --name-status`, rejecting refs that start with `-`) and repeated `--test name,command,passed,failed,skipped`. `render` reads `--report mission-report.jsonld`, `--registry`, `--metrics`, `--operator-level` and writes one `mission-report.html` containing inline CSS, inline SVG and minimal vanilla JS. The page has a header (mission id, status, operator level, timestamp), four KPI figures (duration, files +add ~edit −del, tests passed, autonomy clean-run counter), the Agent workload donut with per-Agent cards, five stage meters (Orchestrator, Data, Analysis, Action, Defense/Audit) with this-run result and window pass rate, and the file accordion. Put the CSS, JS and HTML skeleton constants in `dashboard_template.py`. Rules: Python 3.9+ standard library only (the 1.1.0 mission lost a CI round to a 3.9 crash), `html.escape` on every injected string and attribute, inline script and style hashed into a CSP meta tag, deterministic output when `--generated-at` is given, \"Not recorded\" for any missing figure, never a network reference. Before writing any markup, read Hallmark's `SKILL.md` and its `references/dark-mode.md`, `data-viz.md`, `responsive.md` and `gates.md` directly, since Red Agent has no Skill tool, and obey The Floor: all colours and fonts as tokens at `:root` (background `#0a0c10`, borders `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` at 1px), no `transition: all`, `overflow-x: clip` on `html` and `body`, `:focus-visible` on every control, a `prefers-reduced-motion` fallback, no tracked-capital labels, no gradient, no card inside a card, no emoji icons. Layout is mobile-first from 375px with a capped content width and a multi-column grid on ultra-wide screens. Monospace stack: `\"Geist Mono\",\"JetBrains Mono\",ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace` for all numbers and paths; UI stack starting `Inter,system-ui`.",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:red"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/PotentialActionStatus",
      "result": {
        "@type": "DefinedTerm",
        "name": "acceptance",
        "description": "`py -3 render_dashboard.py render` on the committed v1.1.0 mission files (report jsonld, `.actionboard/registry.json`, a metrics file made by the `metrics` subcommand) writes a single `.html` file under 150 KB that opens offline; running it twice with the same `--generated-at` gives byte-identical output; `grep -E \"https?://|//cdn|@import|<link|<script src|fetch\\(|XMLHttpRequest\"` over the file finds no network reference; a file path containing `<script>` and quotes appears escaped and does not execute; the command exits non-zero with a one-line message when `--report` is missing or unparsable; it runs under Python 3.9."
      },
      "object": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:src/skills/mission-report/scripts/render_dashboard.py"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:src/skills/mission-report/scripts/dashboard_template.py"
        }
      ],
      "additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "name": "dependsOn",
          "value": "urn:voltron:mission:mission-analytics-dashboard-v1-2-0:assignment:1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:mission-analytics-dashboard-v1-2-0:assignment:3",
      "name": "Report-pipeline integration across all CLIs",
      "description": "Wire the generator into the report flow. In `src/skills/mission-report/SKILL.md` add the steps after the JSON-LD is validated: run the `metrics` subcommand, then the `render` subcommand into the mission directory, list `mission-report.html` in `Files created/changed:`, and treat a render failure as a reported defect, never a silent skip. In `src/agents/black-agent.md` record the start time when the user says \"go\", run the report generator at the end of the execution phase for every persisted mission, widen the \"mission documents only\" write rule to include `mission-report.html` and `mission-metrics.json`, and tell Black Agent to run a Hallmark audit of the generated page when the Skill tool is available. In `src/commands/start-mission.md` mention the third output so the flow reads the same on every CLI. In `src/skills/actionboard-devops-mission/assets/mission-report-template.md` note that the dashboard is generated alongside the gate-evidence template. Use only the `{{skills_root}}` and `{{tool:*}}` placeholders the files already use; do not hard-code a Claude path.",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:blue"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/PotentialActionStatus",
      "result": {
        "@type": "DefinedTerm",
        "name": "acceptance",
        "description": "`py -3 scripts/build.py --target all` succeeds; in `dist/claude`, `dist/opencode`, `dist/codex` and `dist/antigravity` the `mission-report` skill and the Black Agent text each name `mission-report.html` and the exact `render_dashboard.py` command with that target's own skills path; the copied script exists under every target's `mission-report/scripts/`; `grep -r \"CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\" dist/codex dist/opencode dist/antigravity` finds nothing new; the existing `tests/build` suite passes or its failures are listed for assignment 4."
      },
      "object": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:src/skills/mission-report/SKILL.md"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:src/agents/black-agent.md"
        },
        {
