    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:mission-analytics-dashboard-v1-2-0:assignment:4",
      "name": "Dashboard tests and security review",
      "description": "Create `tests/report/test_dashboard.py` and fixtures under `tests/report/fixtures/` (a trimmed report jsonld, registry and metrics file, labelled as synthetic). Tests, each failing before the renderer exists: zero external network (parse with `html.parser`; no `http(s):`, protocol-relative or `data:`-wrapped remote URL in any `src`, `href`, `srcset`, `action` or CSS `url()`; no `<link>`, `<iframe>`, `<script src>`, `<img src>` to a remote host, `@import`, `fetch`, `XMLHttpRequest`, `WebSocket`, `sendBeacon`, dynamic `import()`; CSP meta present with `default-src 'none'` and the inline hashes matching the actual script and style); HTML validity (doctype, `lang`, charset, viewport, title, balanced tags using a stack with void elements, unique ids, every `label for` and `aria-controls` target exists, one `h1`, inline SVGs have a `role` and accessible name); escaping (hostile file names, agent text and mission titles are escaped in element and attribute contexts); Hallmark floor checks (every literal colour and `font-family` sits inside the `:root` token block, no `transition: all`, `overflow-x: clip` on `html` and `body`, `:focus-visible` rule present, `prefers-reduced-motion` rule present, no `text-transform: uppercase` combined with `letter-spacing`, no gradient, no emoji); contrast (computed WCAG ratio ≥ 4.5 for text tokens and ≥ 3 for chart colours against `#0a0c10`); no-JS content (every figure and file path present in the markup before any script runs); data honesty (missing metrics print \"Not recorded\", never zero or a made-up value; the \"Autonomous unlocked\" wording appears only for an `autonomous` verdict); determinism; CLI (`metrics` rejects a `--git-base` starting with `-`; `render` fails cleanly on bad input); build (the script is present in all four `dist/` targets). Add a \"Mission report dashboard\" step to `.github/workflows/ci.yml` running `python -m unittest discover -s tests/report -v` on the existing OS and Python matrix (3.9–3.12). Security-review the renderer: HTML and attribute injection from agent-written text, the clipboard handler, CSP strength, output path handling, and git argument injection.",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:yellow"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/PotentialActionStatus",
      "result": {
        "@type": "DefinedTerm",
        "name": "acceptance",
        "description": "`py -3 -m unittest discover -s tests/report -v` passes with at least one test in each group above; the zero-network and escaping tests fail when run against a deliberately broken copy of the renderer that adds a CDN `<link>` or skips escaping; every `tests/` suite that ran before still passes; the security review lists zero open High findings; CI on the pushed branch is green on Windows, macOS and Linux for Python 3.9 to 3.12."
      },
      "object": [
