      "description": "Render the dashboard from the real v1.1.0 mission data (report jsonld, registry, a metrics file whose `git diff --name-status` base is the commit before the 1.1.0 work) into a scratch folder, and load it with headless Chrome or Edge at 375, 768, 1440 and 3840 pixels wide (`--screenshot --window-size`, with `--log-net-log` to list every request). Check at each width: no horizontal scroll, no overlapping or clipped text, touch targets of at least 44 pixels on the 375px view. Also check: the net log shows zero http(s) requests; the accordion opens and the file list is readable with JavaScript disabled; the copy button writes the exact path under `file://`; no console errors; and the page is legible with prefers-reduced-motion on. Save the 1440px and 375px shots as the README preview. Record results; do not fix defects here. If you approve per-site browser access, Black Agent additionally runs the same checks through the browser-actions skill.",
